      "descriptionshorturl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/w/index.php?curid=155024564",
      "extmetadata": {
       "ImageDescription": {
        "value": "This map depicts the ancient Punt region, an area located along the Horn of Africa, which includes parts of modern-day northern Somalia and Djibouti. The map highlights ancient trade routes connecting the Punt region to Egypt and the Arabian Peninsula, showing its strategic importance in ancient commerce. Punt was known for its wealth and for being a major center of trade, especially for valuable goods such as frankincense, myrrh, and other precious resources. The map is based on historical reconstructions and represents the area as it might have appeared during the ancient era. The source of this map is credited to AAR Midnimo originally posted on Flickr and licensed under CC BY 2.0.”",
        "source": "commons-desc-page"
